00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,850
Where on the Moon will a lander have sunlight — and a radio link to Earth?

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,850
MOON DIAL answers it for any landing site, using NASA's SPICE toolkit and DE440 ephemerides.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:14,850
At IM-2, Mons Mouton, the Sun grazes the horizon and Earth is in view 73% of the month.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:19,850
Enter any coordinates: the server computes a new site in about two seconds.

5
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,850
Compare sites and catch blind spots where the crew would lose contact.

6
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,250
Open NASA data, checked against JPL Horizons: largest difference 0.000027°.

